1
00:00:00,450 --> 00:00:04,147
Aarav has three snacks: a
samosa, a banana and a laddoo.

2
00:00:04,147 --> 00:00:07,513
Each morning he packs some
of them in his tiffin box.

3
00:00:07,913 --> 00:00:09,463
Maybe just the samosa.

4
00:00:09,463 --> 00:00:11,618
Maybe the banana and the laddoo.

5
00:00:11,618 --> 00:00:12,818
Maybe all three.

6
00:00:12,818 --> 00:00:15,382
On a busy day, maybe nothing at all.

7
00:00:15,832 --> 00:00:18,753
He wondered about it while
packing his tiffin this morning.

8
00:00:19,103 --> 00:00:23,081
How many different tiffin boxes can
he pack, counting the empty one?

9
00:00:23,581 --> 00:00:26,271
Every box is a subset of his three snacks.

10
00:00:26,271 --> 00:00:29,110
And the set of all those
subsets has a name.

11
00:00:29,110 --> 00:00:30,162
The power set.

12
00:00:30,812 --> 00:00:32,423
First, a quick recall.

13
00:00:32,423 --> 00:00:36,134
A subset of A is a set whose
every element is also in A.

14
00:00:36,484 --> 00:00:39,894
The power set of A is the
set of all the subsets of A.

15
00:00:39,894 --> 00:00:41,298
We write it P of A.

16
00:00:41,698 --> 00:00:42,598
One note.

17
00:00:42,521 --> 00:00:47,224
The current NCERT book no longer has
this topic, but the JEE Main syllabus

18
00:00:47,224 --> 00:00:48,407
still lists it.

19
00:00:48,407 --> 00:00:50,162
So we learn it properly.

20
00:00:50,762 --> 00:00:53,950
Now let us build every
box, one snack at a time.

21
00:00:54,350 --> 00:00:55,795
Start with no snacks.

22
00:00:55,795 --> 00:00:58,309
There is only one box: the empty one.

23
00:00:58,709 --> 00:00:59,905
Add the samosa.

24
00:00:59,905 --> 00:01:03,778
Each box can now go two
ways: without it, or with it.

25
00:01:03,778 --> 00:01:05,288
One box becomes two.

26
00:01:05,688 --> 00:01:06,916
Add the banana.

27
00:01:06,916 --> 00:01:09,266
Again, every box splits in two.

28
00:01:09,266 --> 00:01:10,597
Two becomes four.

29
00:01:10,997 --> 00:01:12,137
Add the laddoo.

30
00:01:12,137 --> 00:01:13,470
Four becomes eight.

31
00:01:13,470 --> 00:01:15,402
Each snack doubles the count.

32
00:01:16,052 --> 00:01:18,826
So three snacks give
two times two times two.

33
00:01:18,826 --> 00:01:22,202
Eight different tiffin boxes,
and one of them is empty.

34
00:01:22,852 --> 00:01:24,489
Why does this always work?

35
00:01:24,889 --> 00:01:25,789
Step one.

36
00:01:25,697 --> 00:01:30,623
Every element faces one yes or no
question: is it in this subset, or not?

37
00:01:31,373 --> 00:01:32,273
Step two.

38
00:01:32,192 --> 00:01:34,707
The choices do not affect each other.

39
00:01:34,707 --> 00:01:37,992
So each new element doubles
the number of subsets.

40
00:01:38,742 --> 00:01:39,709
Step three.

41
00:01:39,709 --> 00:01:43,978
With n elements, that is two,
multiplied by itself n times.

42
00:01:44,728 --> 00:01:48,797
So if A has n elements, P of A
has two to the power n elements.

43
00:01:49,447 --> 00:01:50,483
Side by side.

44
00:01:50,483 --> 00:01:54,428
A has three elements: the samosa,
the banana and the laddoo.

45
00:01:54,828 --> 00:01:58,422
P of A has eight elements, and
every one of them is a set.

46
00:01:58,422 --> 00:02:02,718
The empty set, three sets of one
snack, three pairs, and the full box.

47
00:02:03,318 --> 00:02:04,472
Pause and think.

48
00:02:04,472 --> 00:02:07,042
What is the power set of the empty set?

49
00:02:07,042 --> 00:02:08,009
Is it empty?

50
00:02:11,209 --> 00:02:12,109
Not empty!

51
00:02:12,084 --> 00:02:14,720
The empty set has one subset, itself.

52
00:02:14,720 --> 00:02:17,215
So P of phi has one element, phi.

53
00:02:17,215 --> 00:02:19,348
Two to the power zero is one.

54
00:02:19,998 --> 00:02:21,050
Remember this.

55
00:02:21,050 --> 00:02:23,273
The power set holds every subset.

56
00:02:23,273 --> 00:02:26,834
A set with n elements has
two to the power n subsets.

57
00:02:27,534 --> 00:02:29,270
Now, one worked example.

58
00:02:29,620 --> 00:02:31,239
A is the set one, two.

59
00:02:31,239 --> 00:02:32,535
Write down P of A.

60
00:02:33,035 --> 00:02:33,935
Step one.

61
00:02:33,880 --> 00:02:35,621
Subsets with no element.

62
00:02:35,621 --> 00:02:37,527
Just the empty set, phi.

63
00:02:38,277 --> 00:02:39,177
Step two.

64
00:02:39,087 --> 00:02:40,806
Subsets with one element.

65
00:02:40,806 --> 00:02:44,205
The set containing one,
and the set containing two.

66
00:02:44,955 --> 00:02:45,855
Step three.

67
00:02:45,843 --> 00:02:47,618
Subsets with both elements.

68
00:02:47,618 --> 00:02:50,253
The set one, two, which is A itself.

69
00:02:51,003 --> 00:02:55,179
So P of A is phi, the set one,
the set two, and the set one, two.

70
00:02:55,179 --> 00:02:57,487
Four elements, and two squared is four.

71
00:02:58,137 --> 00:02:59,603
Now, the exam trap.

72
00:02:59,953 --> 00:03:04,239
Asked to list P of A, many students
forget two subsets: the empty set,

73
00:03:04,239 --> 00:03:05,227
and A itself.

74
00:03:05,627 --> 00:03:07,305
Both are always subsets.

75
00:03:07,305 --> 00:03:11,495
Leave them out and three snacks
give only six boxes, not eight.

76
00:03:11,495 --> 00:03:13,898
Always check: two to the power n.

77
00:03:14,548 --> 00:03:15,959
Where is this asked?

78
00:03:15,959 --> 00:03:20,201
In JEE Main, for example in two
thousand twenty and two thousand twenty

79
00:03:20,201 --> 00:03:24,548
four, as questions where one set has
a fixed number of subsets more than

80
00:03:24,548 --> 00:03:25,448
another.

81
00:03:25,821 --> 00:03:26,993
Exam level now.

82
00:03:26,993 --> 00:03:28,425
A has two elements.

83
00:03:28,425 --> 00:03:31,257
How many elements does P of P of A have?

84
00:03:31,257 --> 00:03:32,479
Pause and solve.

85
00:03:37,879 --> 00:03:39,384
The answer is C.

86
00:03:39,384 --> 00:03:40,284
Sixteen.

87
00:03:40,712 --> 00:03:45,051
A has two elements, so P of A has
two squared, which is four elements.

88
00:03:45,551 --> 00:03:49,554
Now P of P of A is the power
set of a set with four elements.

89
00:03:50,054 --> 00:03:52,647
So it has two to the power four elements.

90
00:03:52,647 --> 00:03:53,770
That is sixteen.

91
00:03:54,370 --> 00:03:55,829
Here is your recap.

92
00:03:55,829 --> 00:03:57,328
Screenshot this card.

93
00:04:00,528 --> 00:04:03,365
Can you answer these three
questions without help?

94
00:04:03,765 --> 00:04:04,665
One.

95
00:04:04,247 --> 00:04:07,506
How many subsets does a set
with five elements have?

96
00:04:08,406 --> 00:04:09,306
Two.

97
00:04:08,907 --> 00:04:12,152
Write the power set of
the set containing just a.

98
00:04:13,052 --> 00:04:13,952
Three.

99
00:04:13,649 --> 00:04:16,997
Why is the empty set always
an element of P of A?

100
00:04:18,097 --> 00:04:22,745
Next time: a road sign says speed
twenty to forty kilometres per hour.

101
00:04:22,745 --> 00:04:24,030
Is forty allowed?

102
00:04:24,030 --> 00:04:26,560
We meet intervals on the number line.
